strand-fortran
==============

This project is a modern Fortran numerical translation of strand 0.2.3.
The upstream package was authored by Jeff Enos and David Kane, with
contributions from Ben Czekanski, Robert Hoover, Jack Luby, and Nils Wallin.
The upstream package declares the GNU General Public License version 3.

The translated project preserves that license as GPL-3.0-only. The complete
upstream source supplied by the user is retained unmodified under
original/strand-0.2.3, and the supplied archive is retained under provenance/.

The Fortran translation replaces R6 objects, data frames, YAML configuration,
Arrow/Feather storage, Rglpk/Rsymphony bindings, plotting, Shiny, and reporting
infrastructure with typed array-oriented Fortran interfaces and a native
simplex linear-programming solver. See COVERAGE.md and PORTING_NOTES.md for the
precise computational scope and API differences.
